---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Clinic Management Software in India | Qare.in">
  <div class="mx-auto px-4 py-8 max-w-5xl my-20">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-1 font-bricolage">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-md font-bold text-center">Fair. Transparent. Simple.</p>
    <div class="max-w-5xl flex-1 [&>h2]:text-xl [&>h2]:font-bold [&>p]:mb-6 mx-auto p-10">
      <h2 class="font-bricolage mt-1">1. What Qare Provides</h2>
      <p>
        Qare is a software-as-a-service clinic management platform for appointment scheduling, patient records, billing, and practice operations. 
        The Service is multi-tenant and delivered over the internet. 
        Some features may be in limited availability or change over time.
      </p>
      
      <h2 class="font-bricolage mt-1">2. Using the Service</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to:
      </p>
      
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside mb-6">
        <li>Provide accurate account information and keep it up to date</li>
        <li>Safeguard login credentials and notify us of unauthorized use</li>
        <li>Use the Service in compliance with applicable law and patient privacy obligations</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="font-bricolage mt-1">3. Third‑Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        Qare integrates with third parties you may use, such as Razorpay (payments) and WhatsApp Cloud API (messaging). 
        Your use of those services is governed by their terms. 
        We host our application on cloud infrastructure (e.g., AWS). 
        We do not control third‑party availability or policies.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-bricolage mt-1">4. Subscription and Billing</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside mb-6">
        <li>Paid plans are billed per the pricing page and checkout flow</li>
        <li>Fees are generally non‑refundable except where required by law</li>
        <li>We may change pricing or plan features; material changes will be communicated in advance when feasible</li>
        <li>You may cancel at any time; access continues until the end of the current billing period</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="font-bricolage mt-1">5. Data and Privacy</h2>
      <p>We process your data to provide and improve the Service, including account, 
        billing, and operational logs. Patient data you store is your responsibility as 
        controller; we act as a processor. See our Privacy Policy for details on what 
        we collect and how we handle it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-bricolage mt-1">6. Acceptable Use</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside mb-6">
        <li>No unlawful, harmful, or infringing content</li>
        <li>No attempts to disrupt, probe, or gain unauthorized access</li>
        <li>No misuse of messaging or payment integrations</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="font-bricolage mt-1">7. Availability and Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We aim for high availability but do not guarantee uninterrupted service. 
        We may modify or discontinue features with reasonable notice where possible.
      </p>
      
      <h2 class="font-bricolage mt-1">8. Disclaimers and Liability</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is provided “as is” and “as available.” To the extent permitted by law, 
        Qare is not liable for indirect or consequential damages. 
        Our aggregate liability related to the Service will not exceed the fees paid to us 
        for the 12 months preceding the event giving rise to the claim.
      </p>
      
      <h2 class="font-bricolage mt-1">9. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        You may stop using the Service at any time. We may suspend or terminate access for breach or misuse. 
        Upon termination, we will provide a reasonable opportunity to export your data when requested.      
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-bricolage mt-1">10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For any questions or concerns regarding these Terms, please contact us at 
        <a class="text-brand" href="support@qare.in">support[@]qare.in</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    
  </div>
</Layout>